{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Run the one-time reclaim. **Do not start until A1-A5, A6-0a..0d and Epic B's B6 are closed**,\nA6-0b records a successful deployment/runtime receipt for the live review bot, and a completed\n`reconcile-bridge.yml` run has a `github.sha` descending from the A6-0a merge. The epoch-blind\nwriter risk is closed by direct runtime proofs under quiescence, not by elapsed time. session_log\n**1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Protocol\n1. **Agent** disables `reconcile-bridge.yml` + `reconcile-bridge-canary.yml` (`gh workflow disable`,\n   which also blocks `workflow_dispatch` and therefore `RECONCILE_CONTINUOUS` self-redispatch);\n   **asserts** no reconcile run is in progress (poll `gh run list`, not drain-and-hope); asserts the\n   **Gerrit review queue is empty** — zero sessions stops new pushes, but a patchset pushed just\n   before the window can still have its `LLM-Review` vote fire during it, and every vote writes a\n   ticket; break-glasses `refs/reconciler/{lock,gate}` if held.\n2. **Agent** pauses the AWS `rebar-autodeploy.timer` and the host LaunchAgents\n   `com.navapbc.rebar-worktree-gc` (04:00) and `com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`. It explicitly\n   refreshes the host `rebar` installation from a descendant of the A6-0a merge, records the\n   executable path and version/source, and executes an epoch-mismatch refusal probe with that exact\n   runtime against temporary real clones. It also records the completed descendant\n   `reconcile-bridge.yml` run and successful `git merge-base --is-ancestor` result. These direct\n   observations replace the former 24-hour proxy and prevent the hourly updater from reverting the\n   binary mid-window. **[operator-attested] Operator** confirms **zero active sessions** and all\n   **`rebar-mcp` servers stopped** (a long-running MCP holds an in-process store handle and does\n   not hot-reload). Gerrit needs no separate confirmation: every Gerrit push comes from a session.\n3. **Agent** converges\n\n3. **Agent** converges the local tracker (`fetch` + `reset --hard origin/tickets`, 0-ahead verified).\n   This covers all 48 sibling worktrees at once — their `.tickets-tracker` are **symlinks to the one\n   store**. The four other real trackers on the host point at different GitHub repos.\n4. **Agent** deletes the pre-rewrite ref pins (A6-0d), runs the strip in a fresh **unfiltered** clone,\n   verifies the pre-push assertions, and pushes with **`--force-with-lease`**.\n5. **Agent** asserts non-resurrection: `git merge-base --is-ancestor <old-tip> origin/tickets` is\n   **false**, and no clone-fetched ref has the old tip as an ancestor.\n6. **Agent** converges the review-bot clone over SSM (`fetch && reset --hard origin/tickets` on\n   `/var/gerrit/site/reviewbot-tickets`). Reverts to **[operator-attested]** if the issued AWS\n   credentials do not permit `ssm send-command` against `i-00880b2c7f13527c5`.\n7. **Agent** lands the `enforce_since` re-pin through Gerrit, mapped via the commit-map.\n   `rebar.toml:115` is the only literal SHA in the system; with `require_authenticated = false`\n   (`:106`) `verify_authorship.py:531-550` returns early and never reads it, so there is **no CI\n   deadlock** and the change lands normally. `verify.opcert_enforce_since` is unset.\n8. **Agent** re-enables the GitHub workflows, the AWS timer, and both LaunchAgents.\n9. **Agent** verifies the ACs below and **notifies the operator** that the tickets branch is\n   available for sessions again.\n\n## T11 migration-safety answers\n- **Expand/contract:** yes — A6-0a's reader ships before the epoch value exists; the descendant\n  workflow run, live review-bot refusal probe, and exact host-runtime refusal probe prove deployment\n  directly while every writer is quiesced.\n- **Batching:** n/a, single atomic ref update.\n- **Resumability: NONE, stated.** A force-push is not resumable. Mitigation: all correctness\n  assertions run on the scratch clone **before** publishing, so a wrong graph never reaches origin;\n  the push itself is atomic per-ref.\n- **Dual-write window:** none — the store is quiesced; the epoch guard replaces dual-write as the\n  stale-writer defence.\n- **Rollback:** restore from the A6-0d bundle + `--force-with-lease` back to the old tip. Known\n  limit: rollback re-diverges anything already converged, so consumers must be re-converged in the\n  same order as the forward path. **No event bytes are ever altered** — only commit SHAs — so the\n  rewrite itself cannot lose ticket data.\n- **T4 destructiveness:** an irreversible force-push to the authoritative store of a live system,\n  chosen deliberately to reclaim 92% of the branch, gated on operator-confirmed quiescence, an\n  off-repo bundle, a fail-closed epoch guard, and pre-push assertions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The A6-0a merge SHA, a completed descendant\n      `reconcile-bridge.yml` run id, and successful ancestry result are recorded before publication.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] A6-0b records the deployed review-bot SHA or image digest plus a live\n      epoch-mismatch refusal result from that runtime.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The explicitly refreshed host executable path/version and its successful\n      epoch-mismatch refusal result are recorded before publication.\n- [ ] A fresh **unfiltered** clone of `tickets` is **<=150 MB** (from 1.04 GiB; the measured strip\n      result is ~94 MiB) and `rev-parse HEAD^{tree}` equals the recorded pre-rewrite tip tree.\n      **Holds only because B6 landed first.** Tier: **repo-level measurement**.\n- [ ] Commit count and merge-commit count on `tickets` are **unchanged** versus the pre-rewrite\n      recording (measured at window time, never hardcoded). Tier: **repo assertion**.\n- [ ] `rebar verify-identity --require-authenticated --since <sha> --format json`, run pre-rewrite\n      against the old SHA and post-rewrite against the mapped SHA: the **stderr summary counts** are\n      identical AND the multiset of `(event_uuid, verdict, grandfathered)` from the JSON report is\n      identical **ignoring `commit`**. (JSON mode puts only the report array on stdout and the summary\n      on stderr; the report lists only non-verified events; every `commit` is a rewritten SHA. The\n      command **exits 1** when `enforced_not_verified > 0`, so do not require exit 0.) Tier: **CLI\n      subprocess, both sides**.\n- [ ] After the review bot's first post-window write, `git merge-base --is-ancestor <old-tip>\n      origin/tickets` is **false** and `size-pack` growth is **< 1 MB**. The ancestry assertion is\n      what actually proves non-resurrection. Tier: **repo measurement after an observed vote**.\n- [ ] No ref a default clone fetches has the old tip as an ancestor. Tier: `ls-remote` +\n      `merge-base` loop, computed at window time.\n- [ ] Operator confirmation of zero active sessions and stopped MCP servers is recorded as a comment\n      before step 3. **[operator-attested]**\n- [ ] A reconciler pass completes green after step 8, and `rebar fsck` is clean. Tier: **CLI\n      subprocess**.\n\n## Files\nOperational — no `src/` changes. Uses the A6-0c script and A6-0d helpers; touches `rebar.toml`\n(`enforce_since`) via Gerrit in step 7.\n\nScope: M (operational). Depends on A5, A6-0b, A6-0c, A6-0d, and Epic B's B6."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785780394799458001,"uuid":"bc3dfca3-be2b-4303-9304-1d58294625c8"}